    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d772">

                <pb facs="0876" n="866" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg866"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/10–2848: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Peiping</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Clubb</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-10-28T17:00:00+08:00">October 28, 1948—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 28—8:14 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>403. ReDeptel 1484, October 23 and Tientsin 309.<anchor n="27" xml:id="d772-f1"/>
                    According Embtel 196, October 26,<anchor n="28" xml:id="d772-f2"/> this office’s
                    warning follows text Deptel 469 [<hi rendition="#italic">1469</hi>].<anchor
                        n="29" xml:id="d772-f3"/></p>
                <p>It is proposed, unless contrary instructions are received, to notify concerned
                    Americans by same communication that efforts are being made in absence adequate
                    shipping facilities to arrange for sea transport from Tientsin between November
                    15 and December 1 and asking concerned Americans indicate whether they desire
                    take advantage those facilities; this, of course, assuming such non-emergency
                    warning will be issued by first indicated date.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 403; repeated Nanking 599, Shanghai 413 and Tientsin.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Clubb</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
